$x=-1$" :question/worked-solution "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $h(x)$ at $x=-1.$\n\nLet's start by computing $h(-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(-1) & =-\\sqrt{-(-1)} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}h(x) & =-\\sqrt{-(-1)} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =-1 \\\\  & =h(-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is *not* right-continuous at $x=-1$ since the right-sided limit is *not* equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}h(x) & =1-2(-1) \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3 \\\\  & \\ne h(-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not right-continuous at $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149751/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc36f534-6b27-5619-a29e-9954d0310adb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149751"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141002/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9809a3ec-8b28-5213-9549-ba9ea2deccca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141002/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "441b977a-83f4-5bec-97dc-76677c77ed34" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141002/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "a090d899-95eb-5af0-ab8c-6e