-2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=3$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}h(x) & ={3}^{3}-27 \\\\  & =27-27 \\\\  & =0 \\\\  & =h(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=3$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}h(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =0 \\\\  & =h(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is both left and right-continuous at $x=3,$ which implies that the function is continuous at $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141002/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc36f534-6b27-5619-a29e-9954d0310adb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141002"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141001/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "d168ddbe-eec8-5b44-a6a2-762fd8895e31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141001/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "4ebdcf6c-419b-588f-a2a5-235fb3f876a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141001/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e6ff54dc-8650-5e9f-b100-a66f7792d393" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141001/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "ad263216-6e6c-5e01-9847-17b6cf57e649" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141001/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "0a53b6dc-9455-56a2-b25c-456a33135040" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141001/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "102423a6-0915-59f1-960d-74a13e7355f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141001/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-141001/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-141001/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-141001/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-141001/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-141001/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141001" :question/id #uuid "74a7e125-df8f-5d99-ba9a-8c4c017433e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-141001" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x),$ defined below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2},\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x),\\, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $f(x)$ at $x=1.$\n\nLet's start by computing $f(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=1$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & =-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-1 \\\\  & =f(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=1$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =-1 \\\\  & =f(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is both left and right-continuous at $x=1,$ which implies that the function is continuous at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141001/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc36f534-6b27-5619-a29e-9954d0310adb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141001"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149748/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "6c663699-19af-5851-9e35-60d7bf4ad83e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149748/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "9f17a6d1-19b4-5914-931d-69297a6f873f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149748/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "a26bcd36-d585-52a3-b9da-42a0b68d6674" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149748/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "e3d754e9-6111-5736-8a28-e40ed9e07ada" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149748/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "608f35b2-2c42-5af2-a157-06d318cf358c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149748/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "739ff091-9c32-5ce2-b283-35e69c6f3c47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149748/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-149748/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-149748/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-149748/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-149748/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-149748/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149748" :question/id #uuid "750f6da8-9900-501b-a2e8-50c8c6d4e7d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-149748" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x),$ defined below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x-2, & x\\le 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=4$\n- $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=4$\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=4$" :question/worked-solution "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $f(x)$ at $x=4.$\n\nLet's start by computing $f(4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4) & =4-2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=4,$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}f(x) & =4-2 \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & =f(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=4,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}f(x) & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & =f(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is both left and right-continuous at $x=4,$ which implies that the function is continuous at $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149748/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc36f534-6b27-5619-a29e-9954d0310adb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149748"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104384/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "2bbbbec0-69e9-59d5-a7f5-17b77e4b8475" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104384/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "88a3d696-4d41-5acb-ab74-9a8026fbe42b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104384/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "6cd5cedf-cecc-5d13-afe2-3a17644ff55a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104384/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "89a18239-2638-5837-8d35-a94113f333d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104384/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2fa0c495-c8af-5b84-af59-4fb3cbd2e4a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104384/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "35fe5391-e6d2-5d26-887a-881be8a3bb43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104384/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-104384/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-104384/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-104384/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-104384/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-104384/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104384" :question/id #uuid "c4959073-98d3-5dc2-bb77-936c253ada61" :question/math-academy-id "q-104384" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x),$ defined below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3},\\,\\, & x<2 \\\\ 8,\\,\\, & x=2 \\\\ 2{x}^{2},\\, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=2$\n- $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=2$\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $f(x)$ at $x=2.$\n\nFirst, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=2$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={2}^{3} \\\\  & =8 \\\\  & =f(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=2$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & =2(2)^{2} \\\\  & =8 \\\\  & =f(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is both left and right-continuous at $x=2,$ which implies that the function is continuous at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104384/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25229703-4cfb-5010-ae5c-f6a54503ced3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104384"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141016/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "c1af28fc-0b3b-568b-a788-8961495d7fce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141016/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d6a39789-2d90-5e64-b560-7b2ef01cb2c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141016/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "e445aecb-d2d0-522c-b459-c818c12825bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141016/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "4798e1f9-7017-5c42-87d6-21653296524e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141016/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "9f733129-68e0-5a97-8f06-427cda1840f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141016/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea66bbc0-4ad7-5036-bd2e-3edf6be6fe24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141016/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer-field/choices ["q-141016/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-141016/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-141016/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-141016/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-141016/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141016" :question/id #uuid "4f0105ea-720c-563f-bbbf-9281912e3e4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141016" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $h(x),$ defined below?\n\n$$\nh(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x, & x<\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ 1, & x=\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ 2x, & x>\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n- $h(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n- $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$" :question/worked-solution "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $h(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nFirst, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is *not* left-continuous at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ since the left-sided limit is *not* equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)^{-}}h(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =0 \\\\  & \\ne h(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is *not* right-continuous at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ since the right-sided limit is *not* equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)^{+}}h(x) & =2(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\pi  \\\\  & \\ne h(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For the function to be continuous at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is neither left-continuous nor right-continuous at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141016/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25229703-4cfb-5010-ae5c-f6a54503ced3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141016"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141014/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "dd33debd-ca5a-56bb-b656-44e1146d89e5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141014/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "7df6ae50-e6f8-5e5a-8788-e5a52f7c2575" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141014/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "963c4af2-2473-5d40-be75-9c823b5fb42e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141014/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "91e26639-e7a1-5f0a-aa6b-4ee4702a649b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141014/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "2584ed35-b7b8-5f29-ad91-1e9c93c30af7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141014/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5dcf9cf4-d9b2-5bd0-aa39-446406493ea7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141014/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-141014/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-141014/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-141014/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-141014/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-141014/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141014" :question/id #uuid "c48c3044-df76-5999-8c85-0a92efc32ae2" :question/math-academy-id "q-141014" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $g(x),$ defined below?\n\n$$\ng(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x-1}, & x<0 \\\\ -1, & x=0 \\\\ x+1, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $g(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=0$\n- $g(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=0$\n- $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $g(x)$ at $x=0.$\n\nFirst, we note that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(0)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=0$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}g(x) & =\\frac{1}{0-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =-1 \\\\  & =g(0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is *not* right-continuous at $x=0$ since the right-sided limit is *not* equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}g(x) & =0+1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\  & \\ne g(0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For the function to be continuous at $x=0,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not right-continuous at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141014/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "25229703-4cfb-5010-ae5c-f6a54503ced3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141014"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141012/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "071a9b06-1a6d-5a39-a921-a8c8e2674a30" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141012/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "c36b20d8-c012-59c0-a94b-bbdf049dbd